                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[u]I played this on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers. [/u] I can confirm this game works, but you have to do a Windows 7 compatability fix.  \n\nIt's a wave shooter.  It's a short wave shooter.  It' s a short, mindless wave shooter.  It's almost impossible to die, as long as you swing the bat back around frantically.  It's dark.  Way too dark at that start.  You can't even see the bat.  You see something with an LED light, get it, it's your submachine gun that auto reloads.  Just pray (you don't get bored to death) and spray.\n\nHorror atmosphere?  Nope, more like a dark/shitty atmosphere.  It's not challenging. It's not worth the download.  And as far as holding the grip button .. oh no, I have to hold on to grip to hold on to the gun.  Welcome to immersion in VR.  Geez.  Seriously, out of all the things to dislike about this game, that's not one of them. \n\nReview 3/10.  It's free, it works, kind of.  I would give the student dev an A for effort.  If it's not a student dev, then I would say your talents lay elsewhere.",
